# 239. Children Sum Property in Binary Tree

## APPROACH: CHILDREN SUM PROPERTY (RECURSIVE / DFS)

Idea:
Har internal node ki value uske left aur right child ki values ke sum ke barabar honi chahiye (`node.val == left.val + right.val`).
Missing (`null`) child ko 0 treat karna hai.
Leaf nodes aur null nodes automatically condition satisfy karte hain.

--------------------------------------------------

APPROACH (Recursive / DFS)

1. Base Cases:
   - Agar `root == null` ho, toh property satisfy hoti hai -> `return true`.
   - Agar node leaf ho (`root.left == null && root.right == null`), toh rule automatically satisfied hai -> `return true`.

2. Children Sum Calculate Karo:
   - `int child = 0;`
   - Agar left child present hai, uski value add karo: `child += root.left.val`.
   - Agar right child present hai, uski value add karo: `child += root.right.val`.

3. Condition Check:
   - Current node condition satisfy kare: `root.val == child`
   - Dono left aur right subtrees bhi valid hon:
     `checkChildrenSum(root.left) && checkChildrenSum(root.right)`

4. Agar teeno conditions true hain toh `return true`, warna `return false`.

--------------------------------------------------

EXAMPLE

Tree:
        35
       /  \
     20    15
    /  \   / \
   15   5 10  5

Dry Run:
- Leaves (15, 5, 10, 5) -> All return true
- Node 20: child = 15 + 5 = 20 -> 20 == 20 && true && true -> returns true
- Node 15: child = 10 + 5 = 15 -> 15 == 15 && true && true -> returns true
- Root 35: child = 20 + 15 = 35 -> 35 == 35 && true && true -> returns true

Result: true

--------------------------------------------------

COMPLEXITY

N = Total number of nodes in tree
H = Height of binary tree

Time:
O(N) -> Har node exactly ek baar visit hoti hai (short-circuit mismatch par pehle hi ruk jata hai).

Space:
O(H) -> Recursive call stack height ke barabar memory leta hai.
Worst case (skewed tree): O(N)
Best/Average case (balanced tree): O(log N)

--------------------------------------------------

INTERVIEW POINT

- Critical bug trap: `if (root == null) return true;` hona chahiye, `return false;` nahi. Agar `false` return kar diya, toh jis bhi node ka single child hoga, uske missing doosre child par call jaate hi poora answer galat `false` ban jayega.
- Follow-up problem (Hard variant):
  - Convert an arbitrary binary tree to hold Children Sum Property (jisme tree modify karna allow hota hai without decreasing any node's value).

--------------------------------------------------

# CODE:

// class TreeNode {
//     int val;
//     TreeNode left, right;
//     TreeNode(int x) { val = x; }
// }

class Solution {
    boolean checkChildrenSum(TreeNode root) { 
        // Base Case 1: Null node vacuously satisfies the property
        if (root == null) return true;

        // Base Case 2: Leaf node automatically satisfies the rules
        if (root.left == null && root.right == null) return true;

        int child = 0;
        if (root.left != null) child += root.left.val;
        if (root.right != null) child += root.right.val;

        // Current node match AND both subtrees satisfy the property
        return (root.val == child) 
            && checkChildrenSum(root.left) 
            && checkChildrenSum(root.right);
    }
}
